# DocuMind Principal Android/AI Engineer Rules

Expert Android Engineer standards for DocuMind - Universal AI Reading Assistant with on-device LLM.

## 1. Architecture (Clean + MVVM)

```
app/
├── data/           # Repositories, data sources, extractors
│   ├── llm/        # LlmManager, ModelStatusManager
│   ├── extractor/  # PdfExtractor, DocxExtractor, WebExtractor
│   └── processor/  # ContentProcessor
├── domain/
│   ├── model/      # ContentItem, ChatMessage, ModelState
│   └── usecase/    # Business logic (single responsibility)
├── ui/
│   ├── screens/    # HomeScreen, ReaderScreen, ChatScreen
│   ├── components/ # Reusable composables
│   ├── viewmodel/  # DocuMindViewModel (StateFlow)
│   └── theme/      # Material3 theme, colors
└── util/           # Extensions, helpers
```

- **ViewModel:** Expose `StateFlow` for UI state, `SharedFlow` for one-time events
- **Repository:** Single source of truth; constructor-inject via Hilt
- **UseCase:** One public function per use case

## 2. Jetpack Compose

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD - State in composable
@Composable
fun ChatScreen() {
    var messages by remember { mutableStateOf(listOf<ChatMessage>()) }
}

// ✅ GOOD - Hoisted to ViewModel
@Composable
fun ChatScreen(
    messages: List<ChatMessage>,
    onSendMessage: (String) -> Unit
)
```

- Mark domain models `@Stable` or `@Immutable`
- Use `derivedStateOf` for computed values
- Use `remember { }` for lambdas passed to child composables
- Follow Material 3; use `MaterialTheme.colorScheme`

## 3. On-Device AI (MediaPipe LlmInference)

```kotlin
// ✅ GOOD - Encapsulated AI with Flow streaming
class LlmManager @Inject constructor(
    private val modelStatusManager: ModelStatusManager
) {
    suspend fun generateResponse(prompt: String): Flow<String> = flow {
        llmInference?.generateResponseAsync(prompt)?.collect { emit(it) }
    }.flowOn(Dispatchers.Default)
}
```

- Model file: `gemma3-1b.task` via Play Asset Delivery (`install-time`)
- Always check `ModelState` before AI operations
- Stream responses via `Flow<String>` for real-time UI updates
- Handle `ModelState.Error` gracefully with user feedback

## 4. Coroutines & Flow

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD
GlobalScope.launch { fetchData() }

// ✅ GOOD
viewModelScope.launch {
    contentProcessor.extractContent(uri)
        .catch { emit(Result.failure(it)) }
        .collect { _uiState.update { state -> state.copy(content = it) } }
}
```

- Use `viewModelScope` in ViewModels, `lifecycleScope` in Activities
- Prefer `Flow` over `LiveData` for new code
- Use `flowOn(Dispatchers.IO)` for file/network operations

## 5. Error Handling

```kotlin
// ✅ GOOD - Result wrapper
suspend fun extractPdf(uri: Uri): Result<String> = runCatching {
    withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {
        contentResolver.openInputStream(uri)?.use { stream ->
            PDDocument.load(stream).use { doc ->
                PDFTextStripper().getText(doc)
            }
        } ?: throw IOException("Cannot open file")
    }
}
```

- Use `runCatching` / `Result` for I/O and AI operations
- Never swallow exceptions silently
- Show user-friendly error messages via `UiState.Error`

## 6. Hilt Dependency Injection

```kotlin
// ✅ GOOD - Constructor injection
@HiltViewModel
class DocuMindViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val llmManager: LlmManager,
    private val contentProcessor: ContentProcessor,
    private val analyticsManager: AnalyticsManager
) : ViewModel()
```

- Use `@Singleton` for managers (LlmManager, ModelStatusManager)
- Use `@ActivityRetainedScoped` when Activity context needed
- Provide `@ApplicationContext` for context-dependent classes

## 7. Content Extractors

| Format | Library | Class |
|--------|---------|-------|
| PDF | Apache PDFBox | `PdfExtractor` |
| DOCX | Apache POI | `DocxExtractor` |
| Web | Jsoup | `WebExtractor` |
| Text | Kotlin stdlib | Direct read |

- Return `Result<String>` from extractors
- Handle large files with chunking
- ProGuard: Keep POI/Log4j2 classes (see `proguard-rules.pro`)

## 8. Play Asset Delivery

```kotlin
// Model delivery config (model_pack/build.gradle.kts)
assetPack {
    packName.set("model_pack")
    dynamicDelivery {
        deliveryType.set("install-time")  // Bundled with APK
    }
}
```

- `install-time`: Model bundled (~600MB AAB)
- Track download via `AssetPackStateUpdateListener`
- Verify file existence before reporting `ModelState.Ready`

## 9. Code Quality

- **Logging:** Use `android.util.Log` with TAG; no `println`
- **Nulls:** Strict null-safety; use `?.let { }`, `?: return`
- **Naming:** `camelCase` functions, `PascalCase` classes, `SCREAMING_SNAKE` constants
- **No God classes:** Split large ViewModels by feature

## 10. Testing

```kotlin
// ViewModel test example
@Test
fun `processContent emits success state`() = runTest {
    val viewModel = DocuMindViewModel(mockLlmManager, mockProcessor)
    viewModel.processContent(testUri)
    assertEquals(UiState.Success, viewModel.uiState.value)
}
```

- Unit tests: JUnit5 + MockK
- UI tests: Compose Testing + Espresso
- Test AI responses with mock `LlmManager`
